POSIX_FALLOCATE(2)          BSD System Calls Manual         POSIX_FALLOCATE(2)

NNAAMMEE
     ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee — pre-allocate storage for a range in a file

LLIIBBRRAARRYY
     Standard C Library (libc, -lc)

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ##iinncclluuddee <<ffccnnttll..hh>>

     _i_n_t
     ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee(_i_n_t _f_d, _o_f_f___t _o_f_f_s_e_t, _o_f_f___t _l_e_n);

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Required storage for the range _o_f_f_s_e_t to _o_f_f_s_e_t _+ _l_e_n in the file refer‐
     enced by _f_d is guaranteed to be allocated upon successful return.  That
     is, if ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee() returns successfully, subsequent writes to the
     specified file data will not fail due to lack of free space on the file
     system storage media.  Any existing file data in the specified range is
     unmodified.  If _o_f_f_s_e_t _+ _l_e_n is beyond the current file size, then
     ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee() will adjust the file size to _o_f_f_s_e_t _+ _l_e_n.  Otherwise,
     the file size will not be changed.

     Space allocated by ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee() will be freed by a successful call
     to creat(2) or open(2) that truncates the size of the file.  Space allo‐
     cated via ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee() may be freed by a successful call to
     ftruncate(2) that reduces the file size to a size smaller than _o_f_f_s_e_t _+
     _l_e_n.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee() returns zero.  It returns an error on
     failure, without setting _e_r_r_n_o.

EERRRROORRSS
     Possible failure conditions:

     [EBADF]            The _f_d argument is not a valid file descriptor.

     [EBADF]            The _f_d argument references a file that was opened
                        without write permission.

     [EFBIG]            The value of _o_f_f_s_e_t _+ _l_e_n is greater than the maximum
                        file size.

     [EINTR]            A signal was caught during execution.

     [EINVAL]           The _l_e_n argument was less than or equal to zero, the
                        _o_f_f_s_e_t argument was less than zero, or the operation
                        is not supported by the file system.

     [EIO]              An I/O error occurred while reading from or writing to
                        a file system.

     [EINTEGRITY]       Corrupted data was detected while reading from the
                        file system.

     [ENODEV]           The _f_d argument does not refer to a file that supports
                        ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee.

     [ENOSPC]           There is insufficient free space remaining on the file
                        system storage media.

     [ENOTCAPABLE]      The file descriptor _f_d has insufficient rights.

     [ESPIPE]           The _f_d argument is associated with a pipe or FIFO.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     creat(2), ftruncate(2), open(2), unlink(2)

SSTTAANNDDAARRDDSS
     The ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee() system call conforms to IEEE Std 1003.1-2004
     (“POSIX.1”).

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ppoossiixx__ffaallllooccaattee() function appeared in FreeBSD 9.0.

